<header class="page-header">
  <div class="section-label">04 &mdash; The Door</div>
  <h1>Engage</h1>
  <p class="page-desc">You already know something isn&rsquo;t working. Literary Science is the methodology that makes it real.</p>
</header>

<div class="mirror reveal" style="max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 3rem 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);">
  <p style="font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--warm-gray); margin-bottom: 1.2rem;">Your service learning program looks good in the brochure. Students volunteer, write reflections, feel good. But nothing changes&mdash;not for the community, not for the students. Everyone in the room knows it.</p>
  <p style="font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--warm-gray); margin-bottom: 1.2rem;">Your institution just hired a director of diversity, equity, and inclusion. The person is talented. The role is set up to fail. Because the institution hasn&rsquo;t changed what it&rsquo;s for&mdash;it has added a position and called it progress.</p>
  <p style="font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--warm-gray); margin-bottom: 1.2rem;">Your museum, your library, your campus sits three blocks from a community that has never felt invited. You have the space, the people, the networks, the credibility. The community has knowledge, history, and needs that your programming has never touched. The gate between you is open in theory. In practice, it isn&rsquo;t.</p>
  <p style="font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500;">These are three versions of the same problem. The institution has extraordinary assets. The community has extraordinary knowledge. Nothing connects them at the level of real work, real investment, real power. Literary Science is the methodology that builds that connection&mdash;not as a program you add, but as a transformation of what your space is for.</p>
</div>

<div class="offerings">

  <div class="offering reveal">
    <div class="offering-left">
      <div class="offering-num">01</div>
      <div class="offering-title">Discovery</div>
      <div class="offering-tag">The Starting Point</div>
    </div>
    <div class="offering-right">
      <p class="offering-body">You know something needs to change. You&rsquo;re not sure what the change looks like. We come in, meet your people, observe your programming, and read the space&mdash;what assets are inside the gate, what potential is unrealized, what a real community partnership could look like in your specific environment. You receive a written assessment and an implementation roadmap.</p>
      <p class="offering-body">Discovery is the starting point for institutions that are done with surface-level community engagement and ready to find out what deeper work looks like.</p>
      <div class="offering-formats">
        <span class="format-tag">Site Assessment</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Stakeholder Interviews</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Implementation Roadmap</span>
      </div>
      <div class="offering-cta">
        <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Start Here &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="offering reveal">
    <div class="offering-left">
      <div class="offering-num">02</div>
      <div class="offering-title">Training &amp; Residency</div>
      <div class="offering-tag">Building Capacity</div>
    </div>
    <div class="offering-right">
      <p class="offering-body">We train your teachers, facilitators, and program leaders in the Literary Science methodology&mdash;how to select texts, how to teach through the lens of systems analysis, how to connect literary analysis to community data, how to facilitate hypothesis development. This can include a site visit to NewComm, where Literary Science was born and is practiced at its fullest.</p>
      <p class="offering-body">The goal is not dependence on an outside consultant. It is building your institution&rsquo;s internal capacity to practice Literary Science on your own terms, with your own community, using your own texts.</p>
      <div class="offering-formats">
        <span class="format-tag">Faculty Workshops</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Multi-Day Intensive</span>
        <span class="format-tag">NewComm Site Visit</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Ongoing Coaching</span>
      </div>
      <div class="offering-cta">
        <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Inquire &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="offering reveal">
    <div class="offering-left">
      <div class="offering-num">03</div>
      <div class="offering-title">Institutional Redesign</div>
      <div class="offering-tag">The Deepest Engagement</div>
    </div>
    <div class="offering-right">
      <p class="offering-body">This is not a workshop about the methodology. It is the methodology built into your institution&rsquo;s architecture. We work with you over a full year to reimagine your space&mdash;transforming it from a site of traditional programming into a site of collective knowledge-making, community investment, and shared power.</p>
      <p class="offering-body">For schools, museums, libraries, and cultural institutions ready to ask the harder question: not how do we serve the community, but what becomes possible when we open the gate and build together?</p>
      <div class="offering-formats">
        <span class="format-tag">Program Design</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Curriculum Integration</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Space Reimagination</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Supported Implementation</span>
      </div>
      <div class="offering-cta">
        <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Start a Conversation &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="offering reveal">
    <div class="offering-left">
      <div class="offering-num">04</div>
      <div class="offering-title">Certification</div>
      <div class="offering-tag">First Cohort &mdash; 2027</div>
    </div>
    <div class="offering-right">
      <p class="offering-body">A structured pathway for educators, community organizers, museum professionals, and curriculum designers who want to practice Literary Science independently. Learn the methodology. Teach it. Contribute to its evolution. Certification means you can facilitate Literary Science in your own context, with your own community, using your own texts.</p>
      <div class="offering-formats">
        <span class="format-tag">Practitioner</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Resident</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Fellow</span>
      </div>
      <div class="offering-cta">
        <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Join the Waitlist &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="contact-strip reveal">
  <h2>Let&rsquo;s talk.</h2>
  <p>Whether you&rsquo;re a school ready to reimagine what your campus is for, a museum exploring how to activate your space for community good, or an organization that wants Literary Science in your context&mdash;it starts with a conversation.</p>
  <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">hello@literaryscience.com</a>
</div>

